| Concrete tasks, scenarios and retained input set | SD: Detailed task/scenario mapping and retention inventory | resolved | T-BASE through T-CLOSE, the 20 mapped scenarios and R-RET through R-SCOPE specify actual owners, prerequisites, outputs and unavailable actions; retained input selection is explicit and hash-preserving. | Codex |
| Candidate-bound native cohort | SD: Bounded real-agent execution plan | resolved | One frozen candidate, two unchanged T7 repetitions maximum, CLI 0.163.0 on the observed macOS x64 host, gpt-6.1-sol/low, 600,000 ms each, existing account only, USD 0 additional API spend, unchanged strict audit and no retry/resume/replacement. | Codex |
| Baseline and worktree isolation | TP | resolved | Capture original schema/Core expectations before source edits; use the verified base and an isolated checkout, preserve staging/foreign data and verify actual loaded Core/assembly hashes. | Codex |
| Guard configuration and output import | TP | resolved | Keep the existing settings guard; deny writes under original ROOT in an outer cohort policy, snapshot before launch and compare before importing qualification outputs. No weaker fallback. | Codex |
| Normal build and compatibility freshness | TP | resolved | Use existing build/profile owners; only a diagnosed source_snapshot_changed permits fresh deterministic compatibility recording. Preserve original observations/native inputs and inspect only new owned derived outputs. | Codex |
| Session failure or exhausted budget | TP | resolved | Retain all failures; no additional real session or changed candidate inside this cohort. Report the evidence gap and use the existing explicit TP renewal route if more model execution is requested. | Codex |
